 ],
 "notes": "Single framed modal (bronze frame with corner studs) over a dark map backdrop. Header band: helmet-with-blue-plume icon, gold 'Settings' title (tall S + small caps), castle panorama on the right, red close button top-right inside the frame. Below it a dark wooden tab band with four tabs: Sound is SELECTED (teal fill, glowing gold frame, gold music-note icon, cream label, label sits ~2 px lower and slightly larger than the others); Gameplay/Online/Account are unselected (near-black fill, thin brass frame with corner rivets, grey icon and label). Content: left column is a framed painted illustration (no interaction); right column is a dark panel with the VOLUME heading (uniform caps) over a thin rule with a centre diamond and arrow-tip ends, then four setting rows. Each row is a dark plate with a brass frame and corner rivets, a square icon box on the left sharing the row frame (gold icons: lute+note, crossed swords, wind, bell), a cream label, and on the right either a slider + value box (Music 50%, Effects 85%, Ambience 65%) or, for 'Mute all sound', a toggle switch in the OFF state (knob at the left, unlit dark track, grey 'OFF' text) with no value box. Sliders: brass-rimmed pill track, teal fill, round gold knob; the fill rect runs from the inner track start (x 660) to the knob centre, so fill.w / 347 gives the drawn position (0.50, 0.81, 0.61) - the concept knobs do not exactly match the 85% and 65% labels. Row heights/pitch are slightly irregular in the concept (67/64/64/63 tall). Buttons: RESTORE DEFAULTS is the secondary style (slate-blue fill, brass frame, gold refresh icon, white small-caps label); BACK TO MAP is the primary style (gold/tan fill, dark map-pin icon, near-black small-caps label). Both labels are left-aligned after their icons rather than centred. Concept lettering is narrower/taller than Cinzel, so sizes are width-fitted."
}